abstract: >-
  The Data Processing module of Enabling the Geospatial Turn in the Social
  Sciences teaches the everyday work between collecting and analyzing
  geospatial data: cleaning raw Census, IPEDS and OpenStreetMap data,
  geoprocessing (buffers, overlays, distances and areal weighting), raster
  processing (map algebra, reclassification and zonal statistics) and
  automating repeated steps, each in Python (Google Colab) and in QGIS.
